+# Actual disposable research principal/session source — API review1
+
+Root allocated NEW files only on f155126a95e80139b1b9679c1870ffd66c29360e /
+e129873c435c8b11d2126307a67b604601e7e4b8. Existing read source84093865 unchanged.
+Separate research service certificate/URI, never READ_DATA handle upgrade.
+This source authenticates a lab principal and creates its actual native session;
+it DOES NOT issue Assignment, resources, dispatch, publication or worker proof.
+
+Proposed exact module unified_system.gateway_research_identity, fixed class
+ResearchIdentityBroker. Constructor keyword-only authority, generation, realm_id,
+profile_sha256, server_ssl_context, server_certificate_der, audit_sink.
+authority must be SAME actual Grid ConsulSessionAuthority with its owned real
+HTTP client and server-private ACL token, not a supplied source callback. Root
+qualifies complete source/class/dependency capsule and actual Consul endpoints.
+Root provides loaded server cert/key/context and observes client server-DER pin;
+profile DER alone does not prove the key/cert was loaded.
+
+`async open_session(server_ssl_socket, *, leader) -> ResearchPrincipalContext`
+checks actual same-context server SSLSocket/verified CA/leaf clientAuth EKU/exact
+one URI urn:unified:test:research-service:<UUID>/DER fingerprint and local expiry.
+Loads actual canonical immutable profile and current principal/policy from SAME
+Consul namespace. Creates a genuine native session and atomically acquires its
+principal-session lock with generation/leader/principal/policy/profile index
+checks. Confirms actual stored native session/value/index consistently before
+minting private same-instance context. No caller-provided cert bytes/role/session.
+
+`async capture_current(context, *, scope, request_bytes) -> ResearchIdentityCapture`
+accepts only actual issuer inventory context, actual socket/current clock, fixed
+scope SUBMIT_RESEARCH/READ_RESEARCH/CANCEL_OWN_JOB and original bounded bytes.
+Reads actual current profile/principal/policy/session lock consistently; verifies
+all identity and state/scope/session joins, records exact raw/ModifyIndex/Session.
+Capture is immutable issuer-owned read evidence, not an execution permission.
+
+`ResearchIdentityBroker.require_capture(expected_broker, capture, *,
+expected_authority, scope, request_bytes)` synchronously checks exact types and
+issuer/inventory/authority-instance/operation/digest/local expiry and returns a
+detached immutable snapshot. A2 builds own native index/session checks from it.
+No arbitrary receiver callback/None return or JSON/native-source flag is proof.
+Actual target checks captured principal/policy/profile/session again in mutation.
+
+`async invalidate_context(context)` latches local invalidation BEFORE attempting
+native session destroy; failure/unknown never restores old context. `async close()`
+invalidates only own issued sessions, no foreign process/session enumeration.
+
+## Backend-derived native records, no fake issued rows
+
+N=existing unified/<clusterUUID>; L=N/runtime-v1/research-lab-v1/<realmUUID>/.
+Profile L/profile-registry/<profileSHA>: canonical bytes hash MUST equal selector;
+closed schema unified.authority.research-lab-profile.v1-review1, cluster_id,
+realm_id, principal_registry (peer DER SHA -> actor UUID), input_request_sha256,
+producer_head, resources, expiry_semantics=NATIVE_SESSION_INVALIDATION_NOT_UTC_AT_COMMIT,
+expires_utc. No own profile hash inside body. Root profile commissioning remains
+explicit; fixture may provision legitimate policy/registration, never fake grants.
+
+Principal L/principals/<actorUUID>: closed schema
+unified.authority.research-lab-principal.v1-review1, actor_id, service_id,
+certificate_sha256, quota_owner_id, policy_id, profile_sha256, state ACTIVE/REVOKED.
+Policy L/policies/<policyUUID>: closed schema
+unified.authority.research-lab-policy.v1-review1, policy_id, actor_id,
+profile_sha256, revision positiveu63, state ACTIVE/REVOKED, scopes sorted unique
+subset of the three research scopes, expires_utc. Unknown fields/roles deny.
+
+Principal session L/principal-sessions/<real Consul session UUID>/lock: closed
+schema unified.authority.research-lab-principal-session.v1-review1, actor_id,
+service_id, certificate_sha256, session_id, policy_id, profile_sha256,
+quota_owner_id. Native KV Session MUST equal actual session, positive ModifyIndex.
+Session generated by Consul, not input UUID/fixture-created issued assignment.
+Generation N/commands/generation and leader N/leader are existing shared authority.
+
+Root bootstrap uses actual private Consul ACL credentials, default-deny test
+policy and real negative unauthorized-write evidence. No client policy writer.
+No second registry/leader/job ledger; local dictionaries track process handles
+and native session contexts only. No arbitrary KV endpoint.
+
+## Lifetime and limits
+
+Actual TLS/cert/policy/profile UTC plus real monotonic conservative deadline;
+max15min commissioning, native principal TTL10sec with local safety margin.
+No renewal in first source. Native session invalidation/policy CAS is target-
+authoritative; strict UTC-at-Raft-commit remains P0. Clock uncertainty/late call
+cannot mint context/capture/dispatch; actual known native facts remain separate.
+No new job identity/refund/publish after uncertain outcome. Actor session creation
+can leave an expiring orphan after transport loss; it is not a job/resource grant.
+Audit exact fixed GatewayAuditSink from unchanged read module, Root drains; full
+audit denies mint. Contexts128/captures256, raw record/request16KiB, no default role.
+
+Independent allowed tests: real own disposable mTLS, actual three-voter policy/
+session/ACL primitive under genuine Root commissioning, foreign/copy/callerclaim,
+wrong scope/CA/SAN/EKU, current revocation/session loss/noquorum and audit denial.
+No Assignment/worker/contained-resource qualification follows. Source/owner APIs
+need exact subsequent integration ACK; public Gateway research remains DENY.
