+# Actual broker profile-v2 principal source — runtime review1
+
+New owner branch from31e0351; exact RED predecessord45ae55 source module1e9 before P2 implementation. Current module/test commit qualification is reported separately. These APIs create ONLY genuine disposable research principal sessions and current identity-record captures; no job, worker, resources, publication, result access, dispatch or native-human grant.
+
+Constructor and fixed method signatures remain unchanged: ResearchIdentityBroker(*,authority,generation,realm_id,profile_sha256,server_ssl_context,server_certificate_der,audit_sink); async open_session(actual_server_SSLsocket,*,leader); async capture_current(context,*,scope,request_bytes); fixed ResearchIdentityBroker.require_capture(expected_broker,capture,*,expected_authority,scope,request_bytes). Invalidate and close keep original local latch/native own-session cleanup semantics. Actual same issuer/source/context/private inventories, real owned httpx transport/default-deny ACL, mTLS peer/DER/CA/EKU/SAN and existing Grid authority remain mandatory. READ840 is unchanged; its query literal is unified.query_market_data, not query_time_series.
+
+Added supported profile body schema unified.authority.target-bound-research-profile.v2-review1 from single-job proposal27b169; current v1 behavior remains separate. Exact native outer codec/schema SHA faf01152678c5b066145dcafebe92f593a641a54dac84da3ce1e1df94c0fb261 has exactly20 fields and new native-request schema/mode, no direct conversion. Immutable P is stored in SAME L/profile-registry/S; P has no own S/D, while native13 includes S. Actual principal/policy/session records remain their existing closed v1 formats referring to S. No second identity registry or consensus source.
+
+P2 runtime additionally requires ONE actual fingerprint->actor entry, exact registry/current principal/binding actor and quota joins, cluster/generation/realm, planned job/request/idem, exact producer/input and all20 byte bindings. Strict bounded canonical base64 and SHA retained; decoded target uses its own ASCII canonical codec, exact numeric integer caps (reject bool/3.0 aliases), no duplicates/nonfinite/depth>12. Metadata P/C3 limits still apply; target16KiB does not guarantee expanded P fits16KiB. Root commissioner controls actual profile writes; a caller cannot self-commission from a JSON role/profile/hash. Trial CPU/RSS/output demand strings do not qualify resources.
+
+SUBMIT_RESEARCH and READ_RESEARCH captures for P2 require EXACT original canonical frozen lab13 bytes reconstructed from actual P/S, current actor/quota/generation and fixed input/producer/resources. READ capture does not prove that a planned job exists or issue job/payload access. CANCEL_OWN_JOB capture requires closed cancel12 with its own different request UUID, canonical lab-compatible key and exact original submit UUID/D/planned job/actor/quota/gen/profile. This captures identity for a possible owned cancel command, not an actual cancel/exit/refund. Actual native job owner/original/common binding/CAS is still required in the Grid issuer.
+
+All captures remain read observations: actual target mutation must derive and check ALL captured native record indices/principal-session Session in SAME transaction with real leader/gen/job/worker/hold/resource checks. Fixed require_capture synchronously rechecks original peer/current local UTC+monotonic deadlines and exact bytes/scope/issuer, not a fresh distributed permission read. No serialized object/dataclass/None callback or foreign source is proof.
+
